1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Rules are made to be broken.

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
The Transporter is a action, crime, thriller film directed by Corey Yuen.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Former Special Forces officer Frank Martin will deliver anything to anyone for the
right price, and his no-questions-asked policy puts him in high demand.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
But when he realizes his latest cargo is alive, it sets
in motion a dangerous chain of events.

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
The bound and gagged Lai is being smuggled to France by a shady American businessman, and Frank
works to save her as his own illegal activities are uncovered by a French detective.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Frank Martin, played by Jason Statham.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Lai, played by Shu Qi.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Tarconi, played by François Berléand.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Wall Street, played by Matt Schulze.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Mr Kwai, played by Ric Young.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
Leader, played by Doug Rand.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
The Transporter (French: Le Transporteur) is a 2002 English-language French action film directed by
Louis Leterrier and Corey Yuen from a screenplay by Luc Besson and Robert Mark Kamen.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
It is the first installment in the Transporter franchise and stars Jason Statham in
the title role, alongside Shu Qi, François Berléand and Matt Schulze.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
In the film, Frank Martin, a British mercenary driver living in
France, finds himself involved in a human trafficking plot.

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
The Transporter premiered at the Regency Village Theatre in Los Angeles on October 2, 2002, and was first theatrically released in the United
States on October 11, 2002, by 20th Century Fox, in France on 23 October by EuropaCorp, and in the UK on January 17, 2003.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
It received mixed reviews from critics with praise for its
action sequences and Statham's performance.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
It grossed $43.9 million worldwide and was followed
by a sequel, Transporter 2, in 2005.

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, transporter,
france, human trafficking, organized crime.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The tone is intense.
